3. Third-party material and derivatives
   code/patches/** and code/tbar_patched_sources*/** are modifications of
   the tools released with the subject paper (Xin, Wu, Tang, Liu, Reiss,
   Xuan, "Detecting, Creating, Repairing, and Understanding Indivisible
   Multi-Hunk Bugs", FSE 2024): CatenaD4J / IBugFinder (MIT License,
   copyright 2023 universetraveller) and TBarAPI (TBar, Liu, Koyuncu,
   Kim, Bissyande, ISSTA 2019, as redistributed in the paper artifact).
   They remain under the licenses of their upstream projects and are
   included only as diffs and as the handful of patched source files
   needed to reproduce the study. The tools themselves, Defects4J
   (MIT License), growingBugs (see its repository), GZoltar, and
   Hercules are not redistributed here; the README names the exact
   revisions used.

